course: dictionary
lesson: 2597
title: Departure: leaving, timetables and change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A departure is the act of leaving a place, usually to begin a journey. You will see it on timetables, where the departure time is the time a train, bus or plane sets off.
explain: Timetables use departure and arrival times. A train leaving at 14h05 and arriving at 16h50 takes 2 hours 45 minutes. To find the journey time, subtract the departure time from the arrival time.
explain: At stations and airports, «Departures» on a board shows the trains and flights that are leaving. A departure can also be a change from the usual way of doing something, as in «there was a feeling in the air of change and departure».
fact: Departure means the act of leaving, especially to start a journey.
fact: Departure is a noun, and its verb is depart.
fact: Départ is the French word for departure, and arrivée means arrival.
fact: «Departure time» and «arrival time» together let you work out how long a journey takes.
fact: A «departure lounge» is the waiting area at an airport before your flight leaves.
exercise: A train leaves at 14h05 and arrives at 16h50. How long is the journey? | 3 hours 45 minutes | 1 hour 5 minutes | *2 hours 45 minutes
exercise: At an airport, what does «Departures» show? | Flights that have just landed | Shops and cafés | The weather for the day | *Flights and trains that are leaving
exercise: What is «a departure from tradition»? | A very loud noise | *A change from the usual way of doing something | A trip on a boat | A long wait in a queue
test: Which word is the opposite of departure? | Journey | *Arrival | Timetable | Lounge
test: A bus departs at 09:30 and arrives at 11:15. How long is the journey? | 45 minutes | 1 hour 15 minutes | 2 hours 45 minutes | *1 hour 45 minutes
exam: What does «a new departure» mean? | The start of a holiday | A train leaving the station | *A fresh change from the usual way of doing things | A phone call home
